01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:03.916
And as you all know, we recently
announced a preview of OpenAI GPT models.

01:20:04.276 --> 01:20:09.556
We are thrilled to see how Bedrock
capabilities are helping organizations solve problems

01:20:09.556 --> 01:20:13.036
that matter, because choice actually matters.

01:20:13.596 --> 01:20:19.156
Now these capabilities are already
changing healthcare right here in Singapore.

01:20:20.276 --> 01:20:27.676
Ng Teng Fong General Hospital was dealing
with a common problem chronic disease management.

01:20:27.676 --> 01:20:36.636
That doesn't scale. You know, longitudinal patient specific data,
communication gaps between appointments.

01:20:36.956 --> 01:20:40.516
A model that was entirely clinician led.

01:20:40.836 --> 01:20:47.516
So the team built Project Antenna,
Asia's first population allergy database.

01:20:47.916 --> 01:20:57.596
It uses generative AI and large language models to shift
from clinician led care to patient empowered care.

01:20:58.036 --> 01:21:01.076
AWS provided the database foundation

01:21:01.076 --> 01:21:08.316
and the AI tools LLMs powered
by Bedrock that drive patient communication

01:21:08.316 --> 01:21:11.356
and help the hospital clear regulatory approval.

01:21:11.756 --> 01:21:19.036
Medication adherence went up 50% more patients
discharged from acute hospitals to community care.

01:21:19.316 --> 01:21:23.956
Real cost savings for patients
and for Singapore's health care systems.

01:21:24.276 --> 01:21:27.876
They went from concept to production in weeks,

01:21:28.156 --> 01:21:34.676
and prior content is now the blueprint for managing diabetes,
hypertension, and even dementia.

01:21:35.356 --> 01:21:39.076
So we've seen incredible examples of what agents can do.

01:21:39.596 --> 01:21:43.236
But getting agents to production is still too hard.

01:21:43.996 --> 01:21:47.596
You write your agent logic, but then to give it memory,

01:21:47.956 --> 01:21:54.476
configure identity access controls
and ensure it scales once it is deployed.

01:21:54.716 --> 01:21:59.836
That's a lot to build before your agent even does anything useful.

01:22:00.556 --> 01:22:08.156
For that, we launch Amazon Bedrock AgentCore
to help you go from prototype to production faster.

01:22:08.316 --> 01:22:12.796
It provides a managed runtime with built in memory,

01:22:12.996 --> 01:22:20.636
a unified identity layer for security authentication
to tools, APIs, and data sources.

01:22:20.916 --> 01:22:29.236
Native observability. So you can see what your agent did
and why your agent needed an auto scaling across sessions

01:22:29.236 --> 01:22:34.436
so your agents stay responsive. And with the new AWS Agent registry,

01:22:34.476 --> 01:22:39.956
you can discover existing agents and tools
instead of rebuilding capabilities that already exist.

01:22:40.316 --> 01:22:46.796
Now, what makes AgentCore unique is that it's open and it's modular.

01:22:46.956 --> 01:22:53.916
You can use it with any framework like LangChain,
CrewAI, or strands, and you can connect to any model.

01:22:54.436 --> 01:22:58.196
So we don't force you down a fixed path.

01:22:58.716 --> 01:23:01.516
Again, we understand that choice matters

01:23:02.076 --> 01:23:06.676
because we believe that you should have the power

01:23:06.676 --> 01:23:12.316
to choose the path that works best for each of you.

01:23:12.996 --> 01:23:18.316
Choice matters. A great example
of this is our recent announcement with OpenAI.

01:23:19.036 --> 01:23:25.236
Now Amazon Bedrock Managed agents
powered by OpenAI is a new Bedrock capability.

01:23:25.396 --> 01:23:33.196
Using managed agents, you can quickly build open AI
powered agents that maintain persistent memory across sessions,

01:23:33.236 --> 01:23:37.196
execute multi-step workflows, and take autonomous actions.

01:23:37.636 --> 01:23:42.516
The runtime is engineered to unlock the full
potential of open AI frontier models.

01:23:42.516 --> 01:23:51.556
Using the open AI agent harness. It delivers faster execution,
sharper reasoning, and reliable steering of long running tasks,

01:23:51.756 --> 01:23:58.556
and every agent operates with its own identity,
logs every action for auditability,

01:23:58.556 --> 01:24:02.436
and runs inside your VPC with all inference on Bedrock.

01:24:02.716 --> 01:24:10.636
Bedrock managed agents and Bedrock AgentCore are great examples of why
Amazon Bedrock is the best place to build with AI.

01:24:12.516 --> 01:24:21.156
Now, we actually covered a lot of ground ground
today from Kiro reimagining how we write software

01:24:21.636 --> 01:24:30.916
to agents that secure and operate your applications
to the infrastructure, to the data and inference that power it all.

01:24:31.436 --> 01:24:38.916
And if I take one step back and I think
about what ties all of this together is you,

01:24:40.756 --> 01:24:45.196
and it is your relentless mindset to innovate.

01:24:46.116 --> 01:24:54.956
Everything I shared today is only possible because of the foundation
we have built together over the last 20 years.

01:24:55.316 --> 01:25:00.000
We want to remove every barrier
standing between your imagination and reality.

